# .dockerignore — exclusion-based, per REPO-BASELINE.md §1.
#
# The failure this prevents: every service image build shipping the whole repository
# as build context — the frontend, the tests, the eval corpus, the docs, and the .git
# directory — which slows every build and puts files in the image that have no reason
# to be reachable from a running container.
#
# Rule: this file excludes; each Dockerfile copies only the project files it restores
# and then the source it compiles (P6).

# ─── Source control and CI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.editorconfig
.gitleaks.toml

# ─── Secrets. Belt and braces: these are gitignored, but a developer's working
#     tree is the build context, and an uncommitted .env would otherwise be
#     copied into the image. ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
secrets.env
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key

# ─── IDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vs
.vscode
.idea
*.user
*.suo
*.DS_Store

# ─── Build output — the image builds its own ─────────────────────────────────
**/bin
**/obj
**/TestResults
**/artifacts
**/coverage
**/node_modules

# ─── Not part of any runtime image ───────────────────────────────────────────
docs/
evals/
scripts/
flyio/
tests/
README.md
LICENSE
*.md

# …except the fixtures, which ARE the world the mock workforce tools serve. The
# service links them from evals/fixtures/ rather than keeping a second copy, so
# that the world the scenarios describe and the world the service loads cannot
# drift apart. Re-included after the blanket exclusion above, which is why order
# matters in this file.
!evals/fixtures/
!evals/fixtures/**

# ─── Aspire AppHost: a development-time composition root (P1), never containerized ──
src/AbsenceConcierge.AppHost/
